=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), optionally <Name>.Source.cs, <Name>.ViewModel.cs (the state holder) and <Name>.cs (the
  Fluent view) -- exactly as the sibling W7 TeslaOrdersPage / FleetAPIPage / DevToolsPage do. The generated
  prompt's idealized "TeslaRegionPage.xaml + TeslaRegionPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped
  onto these real conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("TeslaRegion",
  already in RouteTable.cs -> /tesla-region, RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- The web page is a thin wrapper -- `<PageContainer title={t('region.title')} subtitle={t('region.subtitle')}>
  <RegionSettings /></PageContainer>`. The native port reproduces that shell exactly: the page HOSTS the shared
  W3 RegionSettings surface (already implemented under feature-views/RegionSettings, namespace
  TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Settings -- the web also imports the component from features/settings/components)
  inside the native shared-surfaces PageContainer (the parity port of web/src/components/layout/PageContainer.tsx,
  constructed `new PageContainer(localizer, title) { Subtitle, PageContent }`, the TeslaOrdersPage host precedent).
  The RegionSettings component owns the Tesla region / Fleet API card and ALL of its loading / empty / error /
  stale / offline / populated states plus the Refresh action; the page owns only the title + subtitle chrome --
  the two parity strings.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the page parity unit declares NO API data sources of its own (the manifest record:
  "renders from navigation params / local state"); the region data belongs to the hosted RegionSettings (its own
  W3 unit, bound to get_api_v1_tesla_user_region / post_api_v1_tesla_user_region_refresh). Following the
  established host-injection precedent (every feature page's parameterless ctor defaults to an Empty source; an
  explicit ctor accepts the generated-client source for tests/DI), the page hosts the component over
  EmptyRegionSettingsSource by default -- a single successful-but-empty snapshot (LoadStatus.Empty) so the
  component renders its honest empty body ("No region data yet. Click Refresh to fetch from Tesla."), with the
  explicit TeslaRegionPage(IRegionSettingsSource, ILocalizer) ctor for the live RegionSettingsSource. No HTTP
  touches the page.
- The two parity strings resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + English defaults
  (TeslaRegionRegistration.Title/Subtitle -> translation.region.title / translation.region.subtitle). These are
  the SAME web i18n keys the hosted RegionSettings component uses (the web repeats t('region.title') /
  t('region.subtitle') in both the page and the component), and they already exist verbatim in
  Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw -- so NO string-catalog change was needed. The TeslaRegionPageViewModel
  exposes Title/Subtitle and a Reload() that re-resolves them after a language change (react-i18next parity).
- a11y (ADR-015): the page is an AutomationControlType.Group with an AutomationProperties.Name of the resolved
  title; the hosted PageContainer renders the title at heading-level 1 and the RegionSettings component carries
  its own Narrator names (refresh button, cards, freshness/offline chips, live-region notices). Dark/light theming
  + tokens come from the composed shared surfaces (no hardcoded colors). SI units N/A for this admin chrome (the
  region card's fields are region code + Fleet API base URL + sync time -- no unit-bearing quantities).

